Hi Cory

I am writing in response to your Stage 1 Dispute dated 3 August 2026, in wh=
ich you disagree with the decision that has prevented you from attending yo=
ur rostered shifts since 3 July 2026. Your dispute has been lodged in accor=
dance with clause 1.11.2(a) of the Queensland Public Health Sector Certifie=
d Agreement (No. 12) 2025 (EB12).

I wish to acknowledge that clause 1.11.2(a) of EB12 requires that Stage 1 d=
iscussions should be conducted within 24 hours. This letter confirms that y=
our dispute has been received and is currently under review. While every ef=
fort has been made to progress this matter promptly, the 24-hour timeframe =
specified in the clause will not be achieved. Upon completion of the review=
, you will be contacted as soon as practicable to discuss the outcome of yo=
ur dispute and any appropriate next steps. You will also be provided with a=
n opportunity to raise any questions and discuss the matter further as requ=
ired.

Please be advised that I am required to process leave on your behalf for th=
e period 20 July 2026 to 2 August 2026. As at today's date, you have a rema=
ining recreation leave balance of 41.21 hours. Could you please advise whet=
her you would like this recreation leave balance applied to this period? If=
 so, the remaining hours within the fortnight would be recorded as sick lea=
ve without pay. I acknowledge that your dispute includes concerns regarding=
 your leave entitlements. However, pending resolution of the dispute, it is=
 necessary that your absence continues to be managed through the appropriat=
e leave arrangements.

As the payroll cut-off for PP04 is today, I would appreciate your response =
as soon as possible. If I do not receive a response before payroll processi=
ng occurs, I will apply your remaining recreation leave balance to ensure y=
ou receive the available paid leave entitlement for this period.

Employee Assistance
I understand this may be a difficult time for you. Should you wish to seek =
further support, the Employee Assistance Program, provided through TELUS He=
alth on 1800 604 640, is available free of charge for all employees of Metr=
o South Health. This service is a confidential counselling and support serv=
ice.

Should you wish to access this service, please contact TELUS Health on 1800=
 604 640 or for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander support, please conta=
ct 1800 816 152.

More information about the support TELUS Health can provide can be found ou=
t their website https://app.one.telushealth.com/ or by downloading the free=
 TELUS Health One app. You can log on to both using the following credentia=
ls:

Username:      mshhs
Password:       mshhs

Kind regards,
Chloe


